t exports when a specific type filter (e.g. variable only) is set. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66292\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66292</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Prevent WC_Abstract_Order::add_item() from silently overwriting an unsaved item when items are removed and re-added before save() (count()-based temporary key collision). <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/65607\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#65607</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Product CSV importer: respect the store&#8217;s decimal separator setting when parsing weight and dimensions, so comma-separated values (e.g. &#8220;1,5&#8221;) are no longer discarded. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66205\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66205</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Product searches with terms containing &#8221; or &#8221; now apply the include, exclude, status, product type and post type filters to every OR group instead of only a single group, so admin product pickers no longer suggest drafts, excluded products or wrong-type products matched by those groups. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67420\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67420</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Product Summary: apply responsive styles to current and legacy rendered summaries. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67356\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67356</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Rate limit order withdrawal requests by IP address and email. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67069\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67069</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Register legacy block bundle handles as deprecated compatibility placeholders when unified editor assets are enabled. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67055\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67055</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Register WooCommerce block types on demand when a product or variation description is rendered through do_blocks, so dynamic blocks placed in a description no longer render blank in the products REST API, the Store API, the variation AJAX endpoint or product webhooks. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67663\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67663</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Reject duplicate tax IDs in refund line items on the wc/v4 refunds endpoint and the wc/v3 compute_totals path, which previously created refunds whose stored line taxes did not add up to the refund amount. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67613\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67613</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Remove duplicate Shipping settings Marketplace link when shipping recommendations are shown. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66110\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66110</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Remove nofollow from product permalink links in product buttons. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66743\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66743</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Remove Sample badge from sample products generated during the CYS flow <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66322\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66322</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Reorder the cart, mini-cart, and add-to-cart quantity steppers so the decrease button precedes the quantity input in the DOM, matching the visual order for a logical keyboard focus and screen-reader reading sequence. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66670\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66670</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Replace deprecated jQuery .focus() shorthand with .trigger( &#8216;focus&#8217; ) / .on( &#8216;focus&#8217; ) across legacy JS files. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66273\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66273</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Report whether approved download directory rules are enforced in Site Health. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67479\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67479</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Reset stock management and stock status when converting products to grouped or external types. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67484\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67484</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Respect dp parameter when formatting coupon line item discount and discount_tax values in REST API. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66328\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66328</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Respect hidden Date and Status columns on the admin orders list below 782px, so the Columns menu (Screen Options) is honored at every screen width. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66242\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66242</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Respect legacy WooCommerce Admin filters when disabling analytics. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66444\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66444</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Restore and harden the Site Health prompt after approved download directory synchronization. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67491\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67491</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Restore checkout compatibility handling for payment extensions with missing script dependencies. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67365\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67365</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Restore Mini-Cart inner blocks in the Site Editor. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67416\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67416</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Return early in Product block if product is not viewable <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67332\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67332</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Return HTTP 400 instead of 500 for invalid refund_tax and auto-compute inputs on the wc/v3 refunds compute_totals path, by adding the missing HTTP status to five shared-engine validation errors and defaulting status-less engine errors to 400 at the v3 boundary. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67757\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67757</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Serve minified admin scripts only when the minified file actually exists, preventing broken admin pages when the minified-js feature is force-enabled (e.g. via WooCommerce Beta Tester) on builds that do not ship minified JS files. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67515\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67515</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Show the billing name for guest orders in the WooCommerce Home Orders activity panel instead of leaving the name blank. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66279\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66279</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Show the Local Pickup settings save confirmation on a successful save (and an error notice on failure), instead of only when the server response matched the sent payload, which suppressed the notice when values were sanitized (e.g. &#8220;&amp;&#8221; normalized to &#8220;&amp;&#8221;). <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66459\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66459</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Show the Save Draft button when creating a coupon. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66663\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66663</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Skip on-the-fly and background thumbnail regeneration for attachments no image editor supports (e.g. SVGs), preventing PHP notices and repeated doomed resize attempts. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67347\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67347</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Skip the brands product column when the product_brand taxonomy is deregistered <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66410\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66410</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Start new bank accounts on the Direct bank transfer settings page in the business location set on the Payments settings screen. The store base country used before could arrive with a state suffix (&#8220;US:CA&#8221;), which matched no entry in the country field and no routing number format. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67478\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67478</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Stop counting test-mode WooPayments usage &#8211; a test-drive account or test-mode orders &#8211; when determining WooPayments incentives eligibility, so trialing WooPayments no longer disqualifies a store from incentives. Stores already disqualified this way get their eligibility re-determined once. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67154\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67154</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Store API: fall back to the billing address when a checkout request omits the shipping address and the cart needs shipping. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66409\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66409</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Sync trashed and untrashed order status to analytics so trashed orders no longer appear in reports, and remove deleted refunds from analytics lookup tables under HPOS. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/64157\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#64157</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Tighten authorization checks on the Stripe extension install redirect. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66880\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66880</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Tighten moderation checks on order reviews. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66881\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66881</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Tighten multisite site-membership handling during login. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66879\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66879</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Update Checkout total guard to run after addresses in the request have been applied. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67773\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67773</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Use gateway defaults when detecting enabled-state transitions from malformed settings. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66912\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66912</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Use the filename announced by the remote server (Content-Disposition/Content-Type) when force-downloading an external file whose URL has no filename in its path, such as Google Drive links. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66604\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66604</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Use the IPv6-capable ipify endpoint for external IP lookups. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66735\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66735</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Use the selected shipping method name for manually created orders. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66811\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66811</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Use the stable Block Selectors API. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66596\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66596</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Use WooCommerce Analytics to report legacy Select2 usage on storefront pages. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66652\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66652</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; WC_Order_Item_Product::set_product() now resets variation_id to 0 when passed a non-variation product, so reassigning a line item&#8217;s product no longer leaves a stale variation ID that made get_product() return the previous variation. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66734\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66734</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; WP-CLI&#8217;s blueprint command no longer risks a fatal error from loading its class twice. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67074\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67074</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; WP-CLI no longer exits the whole process when the optional wp-cli/extension-command package isn&#8217;t installed. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67074\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67074</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Exclude WordPress editorial notes from the WooCommerce comment count cache, so adding a note no longer inflates the pending comment count shown in wp-admin. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67985\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67985</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Fix Add to Cart + Options redirect when a plugin modifies the form and WooCommerce is installed in a subdirectory <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67798\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67798</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Fix CSV variation import saving a catch-all variation and a stray global attribute when a global-flagged row matches a custom parent attribute. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68002\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68002</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Fix dropdown text and the clear icon running under the chevron in admin single selects on WP 7.0+, including the Order edit Country, State and Customer fields. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67969\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67969</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Fix has_orders_pending_sync() incorrectly returning false when an order changes after a full HPOS backfill <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67838\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67838</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Hide the customer email verification prompt when its email notification is disabled. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67994\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67994</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Prevent REST order updates from failing when a line item&#8217;s variation is deleted mid-update and the posted product resolves to the parent product. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67860\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67860</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Restore the wc_product_meta_lookup join when the Products list is filtered by &#8220;Out of stock&#8221;, so posts_clauses callbacks registered after WooCommerce can still reference the alias. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67890\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67890</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Suppress the customer email verification prompt when guest checkout is disabled. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67968\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67968</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Correct the introductory text on the order withdrawal form. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68125\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68125</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Harden password visibility toggle markup handling. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68176\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68176</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Preserve custom data store cleanup when removing order items. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68144\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68144</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Preserve replacement order items saved by extensions during deferred checkout item deletion. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68103\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68103</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Properly strip tags from product names in AJAX responses <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68175\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68175</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Temporarily disable Helcim payment provider recommendations. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68119\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68119</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Allow product attribute term columns to preserve non-string content. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68273\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68273</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Fix unnecessary repeated processing of fragments in the GraphQL side of the dual API. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68241\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68241</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Harden order line meta value handling in the REST API. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68216\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68216</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Harden REST API key authentication route handling. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68199\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68199</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Improve REST API key authentication for WooCommerce routes reached through custom URLs. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68263\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68263</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Improve WooPayments onboarding profile data handling. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68236\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68236</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Prevent extension gallery markup from breaking variable product add-to-cart forms. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68219\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68219</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Resolve REST API routes the way WordPress does when the request URI has repeated leading slashes or percent-encoded characters. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68237\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68237</a></li>\n<li>Fix &#8211; Restore plain-text product names in AJAX search responses. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/68191\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#68191</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add a &#8220;Send test email&#8221; action to the emails listing page (block email editor). <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66405\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66405</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add a feature-gated public order withdrawal endpoint. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66538\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66538</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add a filter for product attribute taxonomy row actions in the Attributes admin table. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66633\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66633</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add Airwallex to payment providers recommendations in Japan. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67359\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67359</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add an opt-in compute_totals mode to POST /wc/v3/orders/{id}/refunds that computes per-line refund amounts server-side from quantities, validated against the order&#8217;s refund history. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67613\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67613</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add an order withdrawal inbox notification for EU-selling live stores. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67295\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67295</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add a refund preview endpoint (POST /wc/v3/orders/{id}/refunds/preview) that returns server-computed refund totals and per-line breakdowns without creating a refund. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67613\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67613</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add beta support for videos in product galleries. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/65396\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#65396</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add CatalogSortOrder enum class for woocommerce_default_catalog_orderby option values and adopt it in the Product Collection block query builder. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66877\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66877</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add click tracking for the Things to do next task list. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66125\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66125</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add contextual image metadata to onboarding tasks via Task::get_image_url() and Task::get_image_alt(), so third-party tasks can supply their own illustration for My Home and the legacy dashboard setup widget. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66500\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66500</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add coupon validation filters for product_ids, product_categories, sale_items, excluded_items, excluded_product_ids, and excluded_product_categories in WC_Discounts. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/64363\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#64363</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add GoCardless as a recommended payment partner extension for GB (UK) merchants. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/67336\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#67336</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add Helcim to payment method recommendations in the United States and Canada. <a href=\"https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/66960\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">#66960</a></li>\n<li>Add &#8211; Add KOMOJU  &hellip;</li>\n</ul>\n\";s:11:\"screenshots\";s:1035:\"<ol><li><a href=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-1.png?rev=3234504\"><img src=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-1.png?rev=3234504\" alt=\"\"></a></li><li><a href=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-2.png?rev=3234504\"><img src=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-2.png?rev=3234504\" alt=\"\"></a></li><li><a href=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-3.png?rev=3641137\"><img src=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-3.png?rev=3641137\" alt=\"\"></a></li><li><a href=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-4.png?rev=3641137\"><img src=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-4.png?rev=3641137\" alt=\"\"></a></li><li><a href=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-5.png?rev=3234504\"><img src=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-5.png?rev=3234504\" alt=\"\"></a></li><li><a href=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-6.png?rev=3234504\"><img src=\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-6.png?rev=3234504\" alt=\"\"></a></li></ol>\";s:7:\"reviews\";s:17278:\"<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Every release is a new surprise on how it breaks my website.</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"2 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"2\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-empty\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-empty\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-empty\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/sybydesign/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/307766eb54bca9c928d5a7514b55c3316a6128618c0fc07943ed3ebfa1972a50?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/307766eb54bca9c928d5a7514b55c3316a6128618c0fc07943ed3ebfa1972a50?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/sybydesign/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">sybydesign</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">September 3, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>WooCommerce update 11.1.0 – Endless scroll of fixes – because of the endless bugs.<br />They have NO concept of Quality!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Woo was once pretty good. Now, it is endless bugs and abysmal quality.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>4 Stars for function (when it is working).<br />1 Star for quality releases.<br />1 Star for Support.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The worst experience I have ever had with any WordPress related support. 5 weeks of misdirection! So bad, they even sent me an apology.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It\'s bad that they rely so heavily on AI for support - worse that humans don\'t even look to oversee it - and disastrous that they don\'t give the AI current version information. That is totally bone-headed!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I should not be surprised because the software too is released without thinking. Just look at the endless scroll of fixes with release 11.1.0   What will break on my site this time?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Great support</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"5 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"5\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/simonelongato/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/11266e931b9a30aaeeae780c7f75caee6982c8044fcffc63cbdaf196a251234a?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/11266e931b9a30aaeeae780c7f75caee6982c8044fcffc63cbdaf196a251234a?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/simonelongato/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">Simone Longato <small>(simonelongato)</small></a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 26, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I needed support for some errors in the e-commerce site I manage for our clients. They helped us understand the problem so we could fix it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Great Plugin</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"5 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"5\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/abh123/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b03ff597cf83827ff95f87a0c31f5bbeee934df6b84fb00e827dda4ec7be0172?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b03ff597cf83827ff95f87a0c31f5bbeee934df6b84fb00e827dda4ec7be0172?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/abh123/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">abh123</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 23, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is very <strong><em>Great</em></strong> plugin for <strong><em>ecommerce</em></strong> store.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Great plugin, great support</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"5 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"5\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/wonderland32/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/16f9ca6da8b059829ceab9fb4e0937f4289aea3d1ffb317c1bb91b3cf73febef?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/16f9ca6da8b059829ceab9fb4e0937f4289aea3d1ffb317c1bb91b3cf73febef?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/wonderland32/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">wonderland32</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 17, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Glad I chose WooCommerce for my first webshop ever.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Defunct MCP shipped with latest WooCommerce (11.0.1) autoloads and breaks site</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"3 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"3\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-empty\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-empty\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/egsteam/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e0557e1b762c8c1a3b7699cf2b5e6fcb5766b6c2a9135ea3a150017f8f635f0a?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e0557e1b762c8c1a3b7699cf2b5e6fcb5766b6c2a9135ea3a150017f8f635f0a?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/egsteam/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">egsteam</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 15, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I don\'t have any idea why you\'d ship a defunct MCP adapter (0.1) and have it autoload, even if someone has the feature turned off in settings.<br /><br />However, you\'ve broken one of my client\'s sites\' ability to utilize Zapier with their Formidable Forms because Formidable ships its own MCP that is REQUIRED for their Formidable API use (they are currently requiring 5.0&lt;=6.0).<br /><br />Who knows what other API needs other sites have that your darned autoloading is breaking.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Thanks!</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"5 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"5\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/stratocaster/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1f72a61bdbccc42c0c39b2433d043adeeb8bba52539ef9938a478932d8153aee?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1f72a61bdbccc42c0c39b2433d043adeeb8bba52539ef9938a478932d8153aee?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/stratocaster/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">stratocaster</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 14, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Thanks for helping me out!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Billing Region Not Found Woo Commerce - Issue Resolved</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"4 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"4\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-empty\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/jfaulkner78/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/302408bcbfeb405a1ac9aecd40ce1ddf026169bcb335829e624d57fbec0fb3c9?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/302408bcbfeb405a1ac9aecd40ce1ddf026169bcb335829e624d57fbec0fb3c9?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/jfaulkner78/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">jfaulkner78</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 13, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Representative was friendly and provided timely responses.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Powerful, Flexible, and Easy to Customize</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"5 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"5\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/devgirl45/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/dce00f99e4b11877ffe71fbfbd030fa74612a243bc76ba27b5fe87cab8273927?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/dce00f99e4b11877ffe71fbfbd030fa74612a243bc76ba27b5fe87cab8273927?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/devgirl45/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">devgirl45</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 13, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I have been using WooCommerce for around 1.5 years for my business, and overall, it has been a very positive experience. The platform gives me a good level of flexibility and control over my online store. Managing products, orders, customers, payments, and store updates has become quite convenient. I also appreciate the wide range of plugins and integrations available, which makes it easier to add new features as the business grows. The customization options are another major advantage, allowing me to create a store that fits my business requirements. Overall, WooCommerce has been a reliable and practical e-commerce solution for my business.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Thanks to WordPress Team :-)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">A real ace up the sleeve for business!</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"5 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"5\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/colepicoloeliane/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a864263898fe3128190786b9c456b1d121a364f08ee546926fb19dd41efe1207?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a864263898fe3128190786b9c456b1d121a364f08ee546926fb19dd41efe1207?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/colepicoloeliane/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">colepicoloeliane</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 9, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>WooCommerce is, without a doubt, the best sales plugin for WordPress. It helps us market our products and services in a simple, straightforward, and no-nonsense way. Its ease of integration with other tools and vast array of extra features give us true autonomy to manage and scale our own business. It is the ultimate solution for anyone seeking technological and financial independence, allowing you to break free from the grip of rigid e-commerce platforms that charge exorbitant fees and unaffordable monthly rates. I recommend it wholeheartedly!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"review\">\n	<div class=\"review-head\">\n		<div class=\"reviewer-info\">\n			<div class=\"review-title-section\">\n				<h4 class=\"review-title\">Very helpful guidance</h4>\n				<div class=\"star-rating\">\n				<div class=\"wporg-ratings\" aria-label=\"5 out of 5 stars\" data-title-template=\"%s out of 5 stars\" data-rating=\"5\" style=\"color:#ffb900;\"><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span><span class=\"star dashicons dashicons-star-filled\"></span></div>				</div>\n			</div>\n			<p class=\"reviewer\">\n				By <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/kreativ1/\"><img alt=\'\' src=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b30255ae15d813819ab181785e242e4b99e16247c628ae7a8376789a6a9f8b96?s=16&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g\' srcset=\'https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b30255ae15d813819ab181785e242e4b99e16247c628ae7a8376789a6a9f8b96?s=32&#038;d=monsterid&#038;r=g 2x\' class=\'avatar avatar-16 photo\' height=\'16\' width=\'16\' loading=\'lazy\' decoding=\'async\'/></a><a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/kreativ1/\" class=\"reviewer-name\">kreativ1</a> on <span class=\"review-date\">August 5, 2026</span>			</p>\n		</div>\n	</div>\n	<div class=\"review-body\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I was met in a helpful and nice way.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n</div>\n\";}s:17:\"short_description\";s:146:\"Everything you need to launch an online store in days and keep it growing for years. From your first sale to millions in revenue, Woo is with you.\";s:13:\"download_link\";s:61:\"https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/woocommerce.11.1.0.zip\";s:14:\"upgrade_notice\";a:0:{}s:11:\"screenshots\";a:6:{i:1;a:2:{s:3:\"src\";s:64:\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-1.png?rev=3234504\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:2:{s:3:\"src\";s:64:\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-2.png?rev=3234504\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";}i:3;a:2:{s:3:\"src\";s:64:\"https://ps.w.org/woocommerce/assets/screenshot-3.png?rev=3641137\"